{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469492-discussion-of-vicissitude-potential-non-flesh-bone-matter-crafting","id":1469492,"title":"Discussion of Vicissitude potential & non-flesh/bone matter-crafting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-03T06:08:48-08:00","id":1469492,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Discussion of Vicissitude potential & non-flesh/bone matter-crafting","content":"Vicissitude is a unique discipline that begins its influence on the flesh and ends with the elevation of its spiritual Self above the world of matter (or its flesh). Working both scientifically and mystically. Tzimisce is all the same what to sculpt - a man, a vampire, a corpse, an animal, an undead or a worm. All this is good, but here's what is interesting - the ancient Tzimisces can master unique abilities / mutations / control over the flesh.<br /> <br /> As we can see, the vampire is able to change and rebuild the body of the living and non-living (as well as corpses). They can create a plague (remember flaw) or mutate a body, even alter itself into another human or physical object of different sizes (even copying their characteristics).<br /> <b>But can a vampire change plants? What about fungi and bacteria? <i>(I heard about a certain Tzimisce that became a swarm of bacteria and spread throughout the world.)</i> Wood? (</b>What about a dead tree) Eldest liked to mutate into something unknown or into other animals. Somewhere even mentioned something about a moss or a plant. At least he turned (or manifested) into a tree that gave knowledge or some kind of fruit (Connoisseurs of Tzimisce history, remind me of what he did, pls) If cainite can recover from a drop of blood and control the bones of corpses, then can it control inorganic substances? <b>Stones or shellfish enamel?</b> In theory, they grow a zulo-shaped shell and can transform themselves into mollusc.<br /> <br /> <b>What about some chemicals? Or biological substances? Hormones?</b> Yes, an ordinary vampire doesn't care about that (Except for a change in skin color and a number of other higher-level powers), but ghouls or other living creatures can experience the effects on themselves.<br /> <br /> You know, in addition to discussing the skills of the masters of the flesh, I would like to ask about what kind of combined disciplines or advanced disciplines you created for yourself? I mean, a lot of the nightmarish things the Tzimisce do involve the use of 1-3 points. But besides them, there are unique abilities of the elders that allow you to make quick changes, but on the other hand there are not very many of them and they often contain some form of &quot;quick&quot; change of flesh - to rip out skin or create bone scarecrows. I would like to see what ideas (even banal) are running in people's heads. Maybe we'll turn this place into a collection of fan's combo-disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 12-03-2021, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T10:00:56-08:00","id":1469501,"title":"","content":"Diseases would be some kind of Auspex/Vicissitude 9 like job. The lifespan of bacteria is real short and Vicissitude AFAIK doesn't change genetics. You can make the mother beautiful, but she'll still birth ugly children.<br /> <br /> I believe Vicissitude only concerns itself with... Fauna. No plants, no fungus. You'll have better luck with Thaumaturgy/Necromancy/KSorcery. <br /> <br /> Hormones? I think Vicissitude would do a good job in Targeting the organs that produce those, though I believe it'd be easier to cripple or lessen the organ than it would be to improve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T10:55:34-08:00","id":1469507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469492-discussion-of-vicissitude-potential-non-flesh-bone-matter-crafting?p=1469501#post1469501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diseases would be some kind of Auspex/Vicissitude 9 like job.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Flesh Rot is level 7... &amp; Why do they need Auspex when they reach level 9 in Vic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> AFAIK doesn't change genetics </div> </div> </div>At least by RAW it doesn't say that. But there are hints to the contrary. I'm not saying that the Tzimisce can &quot;just&quot; take and change the gene code, but they have a chance to learn something similar (especially if it's mafusail). They can change and control the mystical property of blood, and are also able to change the flesh and give it other properties (transform dog into stone or tree). It looks like gene-changing (except mystical property of blood). Of course, changes at this level will require a certain skill or degree of enlightenment.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T17:32:43-08:00","id":1469543,"title":"","content":"Getting Vic to change genetics, and change plant and fungal life would probably require linking the discipline to some form of blood magic. As others here have posted, RAW Vic cannot do those things. But mix it and blood magic and the sky is the limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T00:51:25-08:00","id":1469568,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Eldest, the incident with the &quot;Tree&quot; includes multiple references to how features of a tree are being imitated but It's still flesh and blood. Someone who has actually read the Dark Ages Tzimisce Clan novel might be able to provide more details. I do vaguely recall some descriptions of the Thing under New York being plant- or fungus-like, not sure. But I always thought that the Eldest was a powerful Koldun, though I'm having trouble finding any clear references now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T09:55:16-08:00","id":1469581,"title":"","content":"The Tzimisce who became a disease was Demdemeh, and he became a virus, at least in theory, it isn't confirmed. Other than that, there's no record of Vicissitude working in non-animal material, or to DNA.<br /> <br /> DNA is relevant only for some purposes. Once we're talking about external induction on phenotype the genetics of the base creature are irrelevant, unless you want to be really nitpicking and actually know genetics enough to understand what you're doing.<br /> <br /> But that said, advanced powers could theoretically do a lot of things with flesh and bones alone. If you can shape the chemical properties of animal tissue, then you can change how this tissue process other substances. We have a number of body components that aren't even organic to begin with, and it isn't impossible for animal tissue to process metals, for example (calcium is a metal).<br /> <br /> Koldunic sorcery is also a factor. As others said, the clan do not have only access to Vicissitude, but also to this form of spirit magic. The combination of advanced Vicissitude and advanced magic can open new horizons. But I do think that advanced powers involving bio-chemistry would make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T20:19:52-08:00","id":1469620,"title":"","content":"It's worth pointing out that Vicissitude is NOT as versatile and expansive as the Life sphere from Mage, nor should it be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T08:25:10-08:00","id":1469646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469492-discussion-of-vicissitude-potential-non-flesh-bone-matter-crafting?p=1469620#post1469620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth pointing out that Vicissitude is NOT as versatile and expansive as the Life sphere from Mage, nor should it be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why the conceptual frame of a Discipline couldn't be as expansive as a Mage Sphere.<br /> <br /> Disciplines are collections of static powers. Their conceptual frame direct the ways the vampire understands and explores the innate magic of the Blood, but ultimately the expression of this concept is in the form of painfully paying a heft price in XP to learn each power, and it only gets to be customizable in fact at Elder levels.<br /> <br /> Comparing it to any Sphere would be as if you had to take a single rote as magic for each dot then explore Archmastery just to have Dynamic Magic, and even then putting an XP cost on every single effect.<br /> <br /> Putting too much versatility on a single <i>power</i> would be a problem, but I don't see the <i>conceptual frame</i> as needing such limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T12:11:11-08:00","id":1469656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469492-discussion-of-vicissitude-potential-non-flesh-bone-matter-crafting?p=1469646#post1469646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why the conceptual frame of a Discipline couldn't be as expansive as a Mage Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me the primary reason not to think like this is because it is very poor storytelling. One of the fundamental differences between Disciplines (and all other linear abilities) and Spheres is that Disciplines are limited and Spheres are not. If you start going around allowing players to leverage their Disciplines so that, given enough XP and enough justification, they can duplicate a Sphere then you might as well throw the whole game out of the window, lore and rules, and replace it with whatever mishmash you want.<br /> <br /> Limitations breed invention and invention is good for interesting stories.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T15:08:26-08:00","id":1469668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469492-discussion-of-vicissitude-potential-non-flesh-bone-matter-crafting?p=1469656#post1469656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disciplines are limited and Spheres are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Precisely. And what makes them so?<br /> <br /> Vicissitude isn't the same as the Sphere of Life and it can't be, because it doesn't work as a Sphere.<br /> <br /> That said, the difference lies in fundamental distinctions on how a vampire relates to the Discipline and draws power from it, a distinction reflected in the completely distinct rules used for those powers.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Not in any conceptual limitation</i></b>.<br /> <br /> Given how Disciplines work, the conceptual frames are of little consequence to their workings from either in or out of character perspective. No one is just imitating a Sphere by paying XP and I didn't propose <i>that</i>.<br /> <br /> Worrying too much with differentiating the conceptual frame of a collection of static powers from a Sphere is, in my opinion, silly because it's worrying with a non-issue. Thinking on top of it that such a stupid difference is what keeps the games relevant or whatever and judging someone else as an ST because of that is just a show of ignorance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}